|                        DICOM_HEAD_TEST                  |
+                                                         +
|                        README                           |
+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+

DICOM_HEAD_TEST consists of few DICOM images, extracted from the DICOM HEAD Project contained in the directory DICOM_HEAD. 

How to use the DICOM_HEAD project in the examples/extended/medical/DICOM:
1) set to 1 the environment variable DICOM_USE_HEAD(export DICOM_USE_HEAD=1). 
2) export DICOM_PATH= path/to/DICOM_LIBRARY/DICOM_HEAD_TEST   
3) The required dicom files, Data.dat, ColourMap.dat are in the directory DICOM_LIBRARY/DICOM_HEAD_TEST. 

Note 1: Use the OLD version of the Metadata files (see point 4a of the README of the DICOM example)

Note 2: The Conversion of Hounsfield numbers to materials (point 5) is not used. The material is associated to the voxel in the Detector Construction 
        without using the calibration curve.This happens because the DICOM project has already been segmented and cleaned from artefacts (see publication).

- ColourMap.dat defines the color of each tissue.
- Data.dat loads 4 DICOM images of the DICOM_HEAD as example. The compression factor is 4.
- 8 materials are defined.
- *.dcm files are the DICOM files of the project


